   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "מַאן דְּתָנֵי ״לִיבָּה״ לָא מִשְׁתַּבַּשׁ – דִּכְתִיב: ״בְּלַבַּת אֵשׁ״. וּמַאן דְּתָנֵי ״נִיבָּה״ לָא מִשְׁתַּבַּשׁ – דִּכְתִיב: ״בּוֹרֵא נִיב שְׂפָתָיִם״.",
   "en": "Rav Naḥman explained: The «one who teaches» using the word «fanned [libba] is not mistaken, as it is written: “With a flame [belabbat] of fire”» (Exodus 3:2), «and» the «one who teaches» using the word «blew [nibba] is not mistaken, as it is written: “He creates the fruit [niv] of the lips”» (Isaiah 57:19), which can be interpreted as referring to the breath of the lips."
  }
 ],
